INSERT INTO `writing_submission` VALUES (1,'2025-11-19 03:36:02.037708','API Error: Failed to submit Task 1: I/O error on POST request for \"https://zoogleal-parsonish-almeda.ngrok-free.dev/writing/1/link\": A connection attempt failed because the connected party did not properly respond after a period of time, or established connection failed because connected host has failed to respond',NULL,'failed','149d7e3a-1700-4813-8490-c674277860a5','2025-11-19 03:35:41.906999','The diagram shows a step-by-step process for producing bricks used in construction. Overall, the procedure follows a linear sequence that begins with raw clay extraction and ends with the delivery of finished bricks to customers.\r\n\r\nThe process starts with clay being dug from the ground using a mechanical digger. The extracted clay is then placed on a metal grid, where larger pieces are broken down while unwanted materials are filtered out. After this, the refined clay is mixed with sand and water to create a workable form. The mixture is then shaped either by using a mould or by passing it through a wire cutter to form uniform brick-sized blocks.\r\n\r\nOnce shaped, the wet bricks enter the drying oven, where they remain for 24 to 48 hours. They then move through two kilns with different temperature ranges: the first operates at moderate heat, and the second reaches much higher temperatures to solidify the bricks. Following the firing stage, the bricks are cooled for several hours in a cooling chamber.\r\n\r\nIn the final steps, the fully hardened bricks are packaged and transported for use in the building industry.',NULL,NULL,187,'There has been a noticeable rise in the use of alternative medicine, and opinions about its effectiveness vary widely. While some people turn to these treatments for cultural or personal reasons, I agree to a large extent that many alternative methods offer limited proven benefits and can pose risks when used improperly.\r\n\r\nOn the one hand, certain alternative practices, such as herbal remedies or acupuncture, may provide relief for minor conditions. Some of these methods have a long history and can complement conventional care when used responsibly. In addition, patients often appreciate the holistic approach that alternative therapy promotes.\r\n\r\nHowever, the main concern is that many of these treatments lack strong scientific evidence. When people rely solely on unproven methods for serious illnesses, they may delay essential medical treatment, leading to harmful outcomes. Some herbal products can also interact dangerously with prescription medications, and unregulated therapies may expose users to unsafe practices.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, while alternative medicine can play a supportive role in some cases, I largely agree that many methods are ineffective and can be dangerous when they replace or interfere with proven medical treatments.\r\nHowever, the main concern is that many of these treatments lack strong scientific evidence. When people rely solely on unproven methods for serious illnesses, they may delay essential medical treatment, leading to harmful outcomes. Some herbal products can also interact dangerously with prescription medications, and unregulated therapies may expose users to unsafe practices.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, while alternative medicine can play a supportive role in some cases, I largely agree that many methods are ineffective and can be dangerous when they replace or interfere with proven medical treatments.',NULL,NULL,273,4,1,1),(2,'2025-11-19 03:36:57.501630','API Error: Failed to submit Task 1: I/O error on POST request for \"https://zoogleal-parsonish-almeda.ngrok-free.dev/writing/1/link\": A connection attempt failed because the connected party did not properly respond after a period of time, or established connection failed because connected host has failed to respond',NULL,'failed','ea6a54b7-f9f3-4055-8cd5-d6fdff9adc1f','2025-11-19 03:36:38.291216','The diagram shows a step-by-step process for producing bricks used in construction. Overall, the procedure follows a linear sequence that begins with raw clay extraction and ends with the delivery of finished bricks to customers.\r\n\r\nThe process starts with clay being dug from the ground using a mechanical digger. The extracted clay is then placed on a metal grid, where larger pieces are broken down while unwanted materials are filtered out. After this, the refined clay is mixed with sand and water to create a workable form. The mixture is then shaped either by using a mould or by passing it through a wire cutter to form uniform brick-sized blocks.\r\n\r\nOnce shaped, the wet bricks enter the drying oven, where they remain for 24 to 48 hours. They then move through two kilns with different temperature ranges: the first operates at moderate heat, and the second reaches much higher temperatures to solidify the bricks. Following the firing stage, the bricks are cooled for several hours in a cooling chamber.\r\n\r\nIn the final steps, the fully hardened bricks are packaged and transported for use in the building industry.',NULL,NULL,187,'There has been a noticeable rise in the use of alternative medicine, and opinions about its effectiveness vary widely. While some people turn to these treatments for cultural or personal reasons, I agree to a large extent that many alternative methods offer limited proven benefits and can pose risks when used improperly.\r\n\r\nOn the one hand, certain alternative practices, such as herbal remedies or acupuncture, may provide relief for minor conditions. Some of these methods have a long history and can complement conventional care when used responsibly. In addition, patients often appreciate the holistic approach that alternative therapy promotes.\r\n\r\nHowever, the main concern is that many of these treatments lack strong scientific evidence. When people rely solely on unproven methods for serious illnesses, they may delay essential medical treatment, leading to harmful outcomes. Some herbal products can also interact dangerously with prescription medications, and unregulated therapies may expose users to unsafe practices.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, while alternative medicine can play a supportive role in some cases, I largely agree that many methods are ineffective and can be dangerous when they replace or interfere with proven medical treatments.\r\nHowever, the main concern is that many of these treatments lack strong scientific evidence. When people rely solely on unproven methods for serious illnesses, they may delay essential medical treatment, leading to harmful outcomes. Some herbal products can also interact dangerously with prescription medications, and unregulated therapies may expose users to unsafe practices.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, while alternative medicine can play a supportive role in some cases, I largely agree that many methods are ineffective and can be dangerous when they replace or interfere with proven medical treatments.',NULL,NULL,273,4,0,1);
